      "handlers": [
        {
          "_baseline_note_raises": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD of `raises` - one refusal ADDED, nothing removed and nothing re-statused. Requirements 17.2 and 28.3, the same pair `PAPER_READ_FAILED` (routers/paper_trading.py) and `MARKETPLACE_READ_FAILED` (backend/marketplace/entitlement_resolver.py) already cite for the same rule. `list_exchanges` selected `exchange_id, updated_at` from `public.exchange_keys`, a column production does not have - the live table carries exactly user_id, exchange_id, encrypted_api_key, encrypted_secret_key, encrypted_password, created_at - so PostgreSQL answered 42703 column exchange_keys.updated_at does not exist on every call, four times in a twelve-hour CloudWatch window. The handler then ran except Exception: keys = [], turning each of those failures into an empty array. An empty array is a statement about the ACCOUNT (there are no exchange credentials stored) and a read that did not complete establishes nothing of the kind, so a trader holding credentials was told they had none and no error surfaced anywhere. The read now answers 503 EXCHANGE_CONNECTIONS_READ_FAILED. The added entry is a REFUSAL being added, not an admission, and no recorded parameter, decorator or success status moved.",
          "_baseline_note_returns": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD of `returns` - the bare `list` entry is REMOVED because the code path that produced it no longer exists, not because a success shape narrowed. That entry was the except Exception: keys = [] fallback returning a plain list; the refusal that replaces it is recorded in `_baseline_note_raises` on this same handler. Requirements 17.2, 28.3. The surviving `computed` entry is the UNCHANGED success return - the connections array a completed read produces. Also part of this change: `last_sync` is gone from each connection object, because a credential row creation time is not a synchronisation time and nothing in this system records when a venue was last synchronised. `connected_at` is now created_at, which it answers faithfully.",
